-- title:
--   Distinct ends have distinct centres on the j-chart algebra
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic and function-field data.** Let $q$ be a prime with $5 \le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` asks for a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$, and `hK` identifies it as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H$ with $N_0 = (q\ell)^2M'$ and $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   **The base ring and the chart algebra.** Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $j$-series [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u \in A$ (`hϖt`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A (↥K) j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) and supersingular in the following sense (`hss`): for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart witness `hArig`.** Let $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the two-chart integral model, the pushout of the two maps from the middle chart to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite and $j^{-1}$-finite chart algebras. The hypothesis `hArig` asserts, for every point $z$ of $X$, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ which is the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258) to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ (`hϖz`) and lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk (`hz`), and every point $y'$ of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.XFin A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L216) $= \operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` (`hy'`) and satisfying the supersingularity condition of `hss` for the ideal $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ (`hss'`), the existence of: a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $= X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion $\mathrm{CMP}$ of the stalk $\mathrm{STK}$ at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1})\,v - f\,u\bigr)$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC} : \mathrm{STK} \to \mathrm{CMP}$ for the completion map, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY} : C \to \mathrm{STK}$ for the germ at $z$ of sections over the `ιFin`-image of $\operatorname{Spec} C$, the following seven clauses hold.
--
--   (1) For $a \in A$, $e$ carries the germ of $a$ to the class of the constant $\sigma(a)$.
--
--   (2) For $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ which is a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$, i.e. satisfies [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) (on the quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H$, $\tau$ realises the substitution by the matrix attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ normalised by $q\ell$, after any embedding $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$), the subalgebra $C$ is stable under $\tau$.
--
--   (3) For $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$ and any such $\tau$ preserving $C$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$.
--
--   (4) For $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and any such $\tau$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ conjugating the map $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ into itself along $\tau$; $\theta$ fixing all constants; $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; $c \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ if $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$; and $c \not\equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity.
--
--   (5) For integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each containing the class of $\sigma\varpi$ and not containing both classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, such that $P_i$ contains the class of $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ for some $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ to the stalk are distinct.
--
--   (6) For a prime $P$ of $S$ containing the class of $\sigma\varpi$, not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$, and containing the class of $X_0 + h$ for some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$: for $a \in C$, the element $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$, viewed in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$, lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$.
--
--   (7) The series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference of this element of $C$ and $a_0$ in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that: for all $a,b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, the value $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit; and $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\text{that difference}))) = \mathrm{mkS}(h)$.
--
--   **A fixed configuration at one point.** A point $z$, an element $\varpi_z$ with `hϖz` and `hz`, a point $y'$ with `hy'`, `hss'` and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`) are fixed, together with data $W_1, \sigma_1$ (`hσ₁`: $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$), $f_1, u_1, v_1$ (`hu₁`, `hv₁` unit; `hf₁` the congruence to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$) and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk at $z$ with $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1})v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts exactly the seven clauses (1)–(7) above for this data.
--
--   **The blow-up algebra and the valuation ring.** Let $J$ be an ideal of $C$; `hJ` states that $J$ is the infimum of all ideals of the form $\tau^{-1}\bigl((e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY})^{-1}(\,(\mathrm{mkS}(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\ \mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\ \mathrm{mkS}(X_1))\,)\bigr)$, where $\gamma$ runs over $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ which preserve $C$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained by restricting scalars from the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : \exists i \in J,\ x\varpi_t = i\}$ (`hB`). Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hR1` has two clauses: $C \le B$, and every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \ne 0$. The hypothesis `hR2` has three clauses: $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. The hypothesis `hR3` has five clauses: the elements of $L$ lying in $W$ are exactly those coming from $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of $C$ lies in $y$ if and only if its image lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and $W$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hEQ` has five clauses. First, for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $= k[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}_q - 1)$ whose vanishing locus is exactly $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$, which is compatible with $A \to k$, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, there is $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\,$[`ModularCurve.FullLevel.redQ q γ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L230)$, c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)\,c^{q+1}$) such that $\rho \circ \tau =$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) of that element applied to $\rho$, and $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$. Second, $B$ is stable under every level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. Third, every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is reached from the branch $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$ by some level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense that $\tau$ maps $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$ into $Q$. Fourth, if $b \in B$ satisfies $\tau(b) \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ for all such $\gamma$ and $\tau$, then $\varpi \mid b$ in $B$. Fifth, a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ that preserves $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Further, [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ (`hjK`) and in $C$ (`hjC`), and an integer $m \ge 1$ is given with $\varpi^m = \varpi_t\,w$ for some unit $w \in A$ (`hm1`, `hmt`).
--
--   **The ends.** Let `ends` be a finite set of subrings of $K$ characterised by `hends`: a subring $O$ lies in `ends` if and only if there is $a \in J$ with nonzero image in $K$ such that, setting $B_a$ to be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ underlying the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : \exists i \in J,\ x a = i\}$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ for which $O$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in B_a$, $h \notin P$, no element of $y$ whose image lies in $O$ is a unit in $O$, and $B$ is not contained in $O$.
--
--   A distinguished end $O \in$ `ends` (`hOmem`) is given, contained in $W$ (`hOW`), local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), containing $C$ (`hCO`) and containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖO`), together with elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u \in O^\times$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak{m}_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto `UVCrossingModel` $\widehat{A}\,(\varpi^m) = \widehat{A}[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \varpi^m)$, where $\widehat A$ is the $\mathfrak{m}_A$-adic completion of $A$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that ring, subject to: $c_xc_y = \varpi^m u$ (`hcxy`); $\iota$ sends the image of each $a \in A$ to the corresponding constant (`hιc`); $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U\,U$ (`hιx`) and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V\,V$ (`hιy`); the image of $c_y$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ (`hcyW`) while that of $c_x$ does not (`hcxW`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $O_1, O_2 \in$ `ends` with $O_1 \ne O_2$, and let $\mathfrak{p}_1 \subset O_1$, $\mathfrak{p}_2 \subset O_2$ be prime ideals (`h𝔭₁`, `h𝔭₂`) containing the image of $\varpi$ whenever it lies in the respective end (`hϖ₁`, `hϖ₂`), and such that for each $i$ there is an element of $y$ whose image, when it lies in $O_i$, is not in $\mathfrak{p}_i$ (`hy₁`, `hy₂`). Then there exists $c \in C$ such that, for any memberships of the image of $c$ in $O_1$ and in $O_2$ (which hold automatically, the ends being localisations of algebras containing $C$), the equivalence '$c \in \mathfrak{p}_1$ if and only if $c \in \mathfrak{p}_2$' fails; that is, $c$ lies in exactly one of the two primes, so that $\mathfrak{p}_1$ and $\mathfrak{p}_2$ have distinct contractions to $C$.
--
--   This is the separation step in the analysis of the blow-up of the two-chart integral model at a supersingular point: two distinct ends of the blow-up, each equipped with a prime over $\varpi$ that misses part of the supersingular maximal ideal $y$ (the Igusa branch of that end), induce distinct primes of the $j$-finite chart algebra, which classically reflects the fact that distinct ends correspond to distinct branches (Igusa components) through the supersingular point. It is obtained from [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.blowupChart_primes_over_supersingular_exceptional_generic_or_end_on_unique_component_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.blowupChart_primes_over_supersingular_exceptional_generic_or_end_on_unique_component_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.forall_ends_exists_not_mem_igusaBranch_of_mem_ends_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.forall_ends_exists_not_mem_igusaBranch_of_mem_ends_linked).
